    "status": "completed",
    "summary": "All repairs complete and verified.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`catalog.py`** — rewrote `read_catalog(stream)` to use `csv.reader`: validates the exact `name,quantity` header (empty input or wrong header → `ValueError('invalid catalog')`), skips blank rows, requires exactly 2 fields per row, strips and rejects empty names (quoted commas/newlines preserved), accepts only nonempty ASCII-digit quantities, aggregates totals per stripped name (zeros retained), and maps `csv.Error` (malformed CSV) to the same ValueError.\n- **`catalog_cli.py`** — `main(argv=None)` defaults to `sys.argv[1:]`; wrong arg count → stderr `usage: catalog_cli.py PATH\\n`, return 2, no stdout. Opens the file `encoding='utf-8', newline=''`; `ValueError` → stderr `invalid catalog\\n`, return 2, no stdout. Success prints `json.dumps(data, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False)` + newline and returns 0. Guard is `sys.exit(main())`.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `python3 -m pytest -q` → 1 passed (test_public.py untouched).\n- Edge-case script: valid (quoted commas/newlines, blank rows, whitespace stripping, zero totals, repeated names, `0005`→5, header-only→`{}`) and invalid (empty input, wrong header case/order, bad width, empty/whitespace name, empty/`-1`/`1.5`/non-ASCII-digit quantity, unclosed quote) all behave as specified.\n- CLI checks: exit codes, exact stderr strings, empty stdout on failures, sorted/non-ASCII JSON output confirmed.\n\nFile-open errors (e.g. missing path) propagate as `FileNotFoundError`, per the out-of-scope clause. Standard library only; no test files modified.",
